From d78e6c3018122d1ab0e5ba17af9f799ba337e8db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim <338195936+tim-meld@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 21:31:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 02/12] metal: small-batch matvec for f32/f16/bf16 rows with
 ne00 % 64 == 0; GGML_METAL_ABLATE switch

1) The mul_mv_ext kernel's thread step is 16*nxpsg elements without a bounds check, so nxpsg = 4
only needs ne00 % 64 == 0; the old gate (ne00 % 128) sent e.g. qwen4exp's hyper-connection gate
(K = 320, bf16) to the per-token matvec, which re-reads the weights for every token.
qwen4exp IQ3_S 24-layer proxy, M2 Max, two interleaved rounds:
pp4 102-103 -> 116 tok/s (+13%), pp8 131-132 -> 153-155 (+17%), pp1 unchanged.
test-backend-ops: MUL_MAT f32/f16/bf16 585/585, model bf16 shapes 18/18.

2) Profiling aid: GGML_METAL_ABLATE="OP[:src0type],..." skips encoding matching nodes, so the
speed-up shows what those ops cost inside the real graph (isolated-op timing misleads).
